                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "malaisante"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "a49f84a7-2f29-4a62-a597-cc1688db8263",
                        "entry_id": "0094cc11-6183-3a9e-9a48-4b7e0738d09e",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "malaisantes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5f53f465-ce8e-3ea0-ae5d-da72ca46f7e5",
                        "entry_id": "0094cc11-6183-3a9e-9a48-4b7e0738d09e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui cause un malaise, une situation d’inconfort face au comportement d’une autre personne ou à un événement incompréhensible."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "France",
                            "Canada",
                            "Belgique",
                            "Suisse"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d33e7f3a-3c14-40f7-bf40-c7c9fd3c0f82",
                                "sense_id": "5f53f465-ce8e-3ea0-ae5d-da72ca46f7e5",
                                "text": "« Ç’aurait été malaisant de parler d’un jeu vidéo alors qu’ils annoncent qu’il y a plein de gens qui meurent. On ne savait pas comment les gens réagiraient. »"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f8ae9ec4-533b-46a5-bfa1-2427df271de5",
                                "sense_id": "5f53f465-ce8e-3ea0-ae5d-da72ca46f7e5",
                                "text": "Gustave Courbet est l’inventeur de ce cadrage malaisant. La légende veut qu’il ait couché avec sa maîtresse avant de la faire poser."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c4a3932-b2cf-4aee-9bbf-148010d3c0ae",
                                "sense_id": "5f53f465-ce8e-3ea0-ae5d-da72ca46f7e5",
                                "text": "Dans La Difficulté d’être ou les Entretiens sur le cinématographe, il déclare que la seule beauté qui vaille est celle de l’accidentel provenant d’un « effet de surprise inexplicablement provoqué par une brèche qui s’ouvre à l’improviste » ; que le merveilleux et la poésie doivent l’« attaquer par embuscade » ; qu’il désire que ses œuvres soient « malaisantes, inopportunes, boiteuses, inconfortables »."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d5c310f5-4383-4ed0-a416-314691033c75",
                                "sense_id": "5f53f465-ce8e-3ea0-ae5d-da72ca46f7e5",
                                "text": "Théâtre minimal de l’évasion et de l’enfermement, Schizes sur le sundae oscille entre confort plaisant et complaisance malaisante […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "14c7736f-1cd9-4eb1-86b0-0a30de48b386",
                                "sense_id": "5f53f465-ce8e-3ea0-ae5d-da72ca46f7e5",
                                "text": "Certains trouvent le style un peu trop carré, mais, depuis le temps qu’on reproche aux politiciens d’avoir la langue de bois, ce serait un peu malaisant de s’en plaindre."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "badd3799-d4e1-44db-bf92-30e78ad1e725",
                        "source_entry_id": "0094cc11-6183-3a9e-9a48-4b7e0738d09e",
                        "source_sense_id": "5f53f465-ce8e-3ea0-ae5d-da72ca46f7e5",
                        "source_sense_description": "Qui cause un malaise",
                        "target_lang_word": "cringy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cringy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bd162e6f-aac7-39fc-a016-fc95b38eea4e",
                                        "entry_id": "28b2c5db-3bd6-371e-ba6f-feb7bad22b5b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative spelling of cringey."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd19dd1e-e73b-4e4e-b387-5396864f1fe5",
                                                "sense_id": "bd162e6f-aac7-39fc-a016-fc95b38eea4e",
                                                "text": "The series features a fantastic, cringy scene set at the upfronts, and the whole show serves as an excavation of the prime-time TV life, from the high-flying ‘80s to the mystifying nows."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7268af31-1768-481c-a0cf-be9b9aef12cc",
                                                "sense_id": "bd162e6f-aac7-39fc-a016-fc95b38eea4e",
                                                "text": "It involved such a cringy mix of self-indulgence and vulnerability I didn't feel equipped."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b7ef448-b26f-4441-9108-38b14568bccf",
                                                "sense_id": "bd162e6f-aac7-39fc-a016-fc95b38eea4e",
                                                "text": "'You're damn right I am,' declares Ron in a cringy American accent, grabbing Andrea in a showy embrace."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91a4d671-3352-445f-a681-ee7a82887d6e",
                                                "sense_id": "bd162e6f-aac7-39fc-a016-fc95b38eea4e",
                                                "text": "There stepped into view a man whom Glen had not seen before. He was evidently associated with Mr. Jervice, but he did not in the least resemble him, for instead of being a cringy weakling, he was big and strong and hard."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f56b4437-ab8f-4aee-826b-09cb5296a464",
                                                "sense_id": "bd162e6f-aac7-39fc-a016-fc95b38eea4e",
                                                "text": "Possibly the thing had feelings of its own; there was no knowing. Just the little cringy sort that might inveigle itself . . ."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2986ea34-7d71-4780-8c7c-38f4d3872759",
                        "source_entry_id": "0094cc11-6183-3a9e-9a48-4b7e0738d09e",
                        "source_sense_id": "5f53f465-ce8e-3ea0-ae5d-da72ca46f7e5",
